  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 148 AM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nBy Thursday, ridge amplification will be underway. The high pressure \ncenter will shift southward over the Great Lakes. As a result, highs \nin the mid 60s to low 70s are expected. Occasional cloud chances \neach day may help temper the gradual 1-2 degree increase each day. \nHowever, while above normal temperatures are expected to continue \nthrough the weekend, a warm and dry but dreary day may be in store \nfor at least part of the weekend as warm conveyor belt processes \nahead of an approaching shortwave trough may lead to increased cloud \ncover.\n\nHowever, there is sizable uncertainty regarding whether this \nshortwave trough will impact the CWA and if so, when that would \noccur. Guidance continues to be divided on the track and timing of \nthis trough, with the majority of models and ensembles favoring a \nslower track with any impacts arriving Monday or later. The \nexception to this is the GEFS and GFS, which favor a quicker \nprogression with the trough reaching the forecast area by Sunday. As \na result, while it appears likely that above normal temperatures \nwill continue, there is low confidence on whether we receive \nmeasurable precipitation or continue with this stretch of dry \nweather.",
